    "definitions": {
      "short": "love.",
      "usage": "love.",
      "full": "H160. ahabah אַהֲבָה noun feminine love (= Infinitive of אהב q. v.) &#8212; absolute ׳א Prov 10:12 18 t.; construct אַהֲבַת Jer 2:2-3 t.; suffix אַהֲבָתִי Psa 109:4 ; 109:5 ; אַהֲבָֽתְךָ 2Sam 1:26 ; אַהֲבָתוֺ Isa 63:9 ; Zeph 3:17 ; אַהֲבָתָהּ Prov 5:19 ; אַהֲבָתָם Eccl 9:6 — love , especially Wisdom Literature & late. 1 human (to human object) absolute Eccl 9:1 , 6 (both || שִׂנְאָה ) so Prov 10:12 ; 15:17 ; compare 27:5 ; see also 17:9 ; of man toward man Psa 109:4 ; 109:5 ; love for one's self ( נַפְשׁוֺ ) 1Sam 20:17 ; between man & woman Song 2:4-5 , 5:8 ; 8:6-7 , (twice in verse); Prov 5:19 compare also 2Sam 1:26 ( ׳א נָשִׁים ); personified Song 2:7 ; 3:5 ; 7:7 ; 8:4 ; compare figurative use 3:10 ; of mere sexual desire 2Sam 13:15 ; figurative of Jerusalem's love to ׳י Jer 2:2 ( ׳א כְּלוּלֹתַיִח ), & of love of adulter. Jesus. 2:33 . 2 God's love to his people Hosea 11:4 ( א ׳עֲבֹתוֺת ) Jer 31:3 ; Isa 63:9 ; Zeph 3:17 . אהד (= אחד ? see Thes.)",
